#!/usr/bin/env python3
# section: 1
"""hee-gen-skills: generate agent-readable SKILL.md from Skill objects.

Real trigger (2026-09-02, Spencer): "do we have any skill objects yet? we
should by now. want to use them to convert into skills file that agents can
read (downstream by design)."

The downstream already existed, built once by hand:

    hee/skills/ratify-contract-v1.skill.yaml     the Skill object
    .claude/skills/ratify-contract/SKILL.md      the agent-readable form

That SKILL.md even names the relationship -- "source of truth is
hee/skills/ratify-contract-v1.skill.yaml. This packages that same procedure
so it is discoverable without already knowing the doctrine file exists."

What was missing is the generator. A hand-kept restatement drifts the moment
either side changes, and this org has hit that exact failure three times in
one day: bootstrap.mk help, hee-ticket ACTIONS, and the glossary. One Skill
exists today, so writing this now costs little; at ten it would be a
migration.

## Same principle as hee-gen-manpages, different source

Pure extraction, deterministic from the object, never hand-authored at the
destination. Re-run any time a Skill changes.

## Why a sibling rather than an extension

hee-gen-manpages is the closest existing tool and the right conceptual
home, but its name says manpages. Teaching it to emit SKILL.md would make
that name inaccurate, which is the same "field that claims something it
does not do" defect this org has been filing against other tools all day.
This lands in the established `gen-*` namespace instead of inventing a new
concept. Flagged for review rather than decided silently.

## Two trees, one generator (2026-10-22)

Until this revision the tool read hee/skills/ and wrote .claude/skills/
relative to ITS OWN INSTALL PATH, so it could only ever render the engine's
skills -- the same install-path bug hee-name carried (fleet-ops#882). A
fleet keeps its own skills in its own repo (fleet rule 7: fleet state stays
in the fleet), so the repo is now resolved from where you run it, like
hee ticket and hee worktree, or named with --repo.

The second change is the ephemeral skill. A software-factory job sometimes
needs a procedure written for that one ticket and nothing else. Claude Code
loads skills from a job's own --add-dir directory, so such an object is
rendered with --skill into the job and never committed to a repo's
.claude/skills/. The object carries metadata.labels.ephemeral: "true" and
names its ticket as the evidence; this tool refuses it in the ratified tree.

SYNOPSIS
  hee-gen-skills [--write] [--repo DIR] [--out DIR]
  hee-gen-skills --skill FILE [--skill FILE ...] --out DIR [--write]
  hee-gen-skills help

DESCRIPTION
  Reads every kind: Skill object under <repo>/hee/skills/ and renders one
  SKILL.md per skill into <repo>/.claude/skills/<name>/. The repo is --repo
  DIR, else the git repository the current directory is inside, else the
  engine checkout this tool is installed in.

  --skill FILE renders one object from anywhere -- a job directory, a
  ticket's attachment -- into --out DIR/<name>/SKILL.md, and is the only
  way an ephemeral skill is rendered. Point a job's --add-dir at DIR's
  parent and Claude Code loads it for that run only.

  Dry run by default. --write is required to touch the filesystem, matching
  hee-gen-manpages, so an accidental invocation cannot rewrite agent
  instructions.

  The object's spec.agent_brief.frontmatter map is copied into the SKILL.md
  frontmatter as given: disable-model-invocation, user-invocable,
  allowed-tools, context, paths, arguments. Any other key is emitted with a
  warning, since Claude Code ignores what it does not know.

OPTIONS
  --write        apply; without it nothing is written
  --repo DIR     the repository whose hee/skills/ and .claude/skills/ to use
  --out DIR      write under DIR instead of <repo>/.claude/skills/; required
                 with --skill
  --skill FILE   render this one object (repeatable) instead of scanning

EXAMPLES
  $ hee gen-skills   # ci
  $ hee gen-skills --repo ~/git/fleet-ops
  $ hee gen-skills --skill tests/fixtures/skills/job-skill.skill.yaml --out tests/fixtures/skills/rendered   # ci
  $ hee gen-skills --skill pve/agents/jobs/NAME/skill.yaml --out pve/agents/jobs/NAME/in/.claude/skills --write

  A bare run is a dry run and writes nothing (exit 0 unchanged, 1 if --write
  would apply differences); --write rewrites the destination and is
  unmarked. The two # ci lines compare against committed output.

EXIT STATUS
  0 OK        generated, or dry run completed with no differences
  1 WARNING   dry run found differences that --write would apply
  2 CRITICAL  a Skill object is malformed, unreadable, or ephemeral in the
              ratified tree
  3 UNKNOWN   pyyaml missing, no hee/skills directory, or bad usage
"""
import subprocess
import sys
from pathlib import Path

sys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent.parent / "library" / "py"))
try:
    from hee_cli import help_wanted, note_ignored
except ImportError:
    def help_wanted(a): return any(x in ("help", "--help", "-h") for x in a)
    def note_ignored(a): pass

try:
    import yaml
except ImportError:
    print("hee-gen-skills: requires pyyaml", file=sys.stderr)
    sys.exit(3)

INSTALL_ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent.parent

# The frontmatter keys Claude Code documents for SKILL.md (code.claude.com,
# skills, read 2026-10-22). Anything else is passed through with a warning.
FRONTMATTER_KEYS = ("disable-model-invocation", "user-invocable", "allowed-tools",
                    "context", "paths", "arguments")


def as_lines(v, indent=""):
    """Render a spec value as markdown, whatever shape it came in as.

    Skill spec fields are deliberately loose -- procedure is a dict with a
    script and steps, prerequisites is a list, verification is a string.
    Rendering by SHAPE rather than by field name means a new field appears
    in the output without editing this tool.
    """
    out = []
    if isinstance(v, str):
        out.append(f"{indent}{v}")
    elif isinstance(v, list):
        for item in v:
            if isinstance(item, str):
                out.append(f"{indent}- {item}")
            else:
                out.extend(as_lines(item, indent + "  "))
    elif isinstance(v, dict):
        for k, sub in v.items():
            label = k.replace("_", " ")
            if isinstance(sub, str):
                out.append(f"{indent}- **{label}**: {sub}")
            else:
                out.append(f"{indent}- **{label}**:")
                out.extend(as_lines(sub, indent + "  "))
    else:
        out.append(f"{indent}{v}")
    return out


def render_procedure(proc, brief):
    """Render numbered steps with their commands as fenced blocks.

    Generic shape-rendering flattens this into a bullet list and loses the
    thing that matters: an agent can COPY a fenced command and can only
    paraphrase a sentence that mentions one. Procedure earns a special case
    because it is the only field whose content is meant to be executed.
    """
    out = []
    ordering = proc.get("ordering") or brief.get("imperative")
    if ordering:
        out.append(f"**{ordering.strip()}**")
        out.append("")
    if proc.get("script"):
        out.append(f"Script: `{proc['script']}`")
        out.append("")
    for n, step in enumerate(proc.get("steps") or [], 1):
        if isinstance(step, str):
            out.append(f"{n}. {step}")
            continue
        out.append(f"{n}. {step.get('do','').strip()}")
        if step.get("run"):
            out.append("")
            out.append("   ```sh")
            out.append(f"   {step['run']}")
            out.append("   ```")
        out.append("")
    return out


HEADINGS = {
    "trigger": "When to use this",
    "prerequisites": "Before you start",
    "procedure": "Procedure",
    "verification": "How to verify it worked",
    "evidence": "Evidence this is real",
    "known_gaps": "Known gaps",
}


def skill_name(doc):
    # The agent-facing name drops the version suffix: a skill is invoked by
    # what it does, not by which revision of the object described it.
    return doc.get("metadata", {}).get("name", "").removesuffix("-v1")


def is_ephemeral(doc):
    labels = (doc.get("metadata") or {}).get("labels") or {}
    return str(labels.get("ephemeral", "")).lower() == "true"


def frontmatter_extra(brief, src):
    """The documented Claude Code keys, as the object wrote them."""
    out = []
    extra = brief.get("frontmatter") or {}
    if not isinstance(extra, dict):
        raise TypeError(f"{src}: spec.agent_brief.frontmatter must be a map")
    for k, v in extra.items():
        if k in ("name", "description"):
            raise ValueError(f"{src}: frontmatter.{k} is derived from the object, not set")
        if k not in FRONTMATTER_KEYS:
            print(f"hee-gen-skills: {src}: frontmatter key '{k}' is not one Claude Code documents; "
                  "emitted anyway", file=sys.stderr)
        # A list renders flow style (`allowed-tools: [Read, Edit]`), a scalar
        # renders as `key: value`; safe_dump's default_flow_style=None would
        # wrap a scalar map in braces, which Claude Code reads as no key at all.
        # default_flow_style=None keeps the map in block style and the list
        # in flow style; for a scalar it would wrap the map in braces, which
        # Claude Code reads as no key at all, so a scalar gets False.
        style = None if isinstance(v, (list, tuple)) else False
        rendered = yaml.safe_dump({k: v}, default_flow_style=style,
                                  sort_keys=False, width=10_000).rstrip("\n")
        out.append(rendered)
    return out


def render(doc, src):
    md = doc.get("metadata", {})
    spec = doc.get("spec", {})
    name = skill_name(doc)

    # agent_brief exists because the first version of this generator produced
    # a WORSE file than the hand-written SKILL.md it replaced. The object held
    # the same information declaratively and none of the imperative framing an
    # agent needs. Generation was lossy by construction, so the fix went into
    # the object rather than becoming a special case here.
    brief = spec.get("agent_brief") or {}
    desc = (brief.get("one_liner")
            or (md.get("description") or "")).replace("\n", " ").strip()
    title = brief.get("title") or name.replace("-", " ").title()

    out = ["---", f"name: {name}", f"description: {desc}"]
    out.extend(frontmatter_extra(brief, src))
    out.extend(["---", ""])
    out.append(f"# {title}")
    out.append("")
    if is_ephemeral(doc):
        ticket = (spec.get("ephemeral") or {}).get("ticket") or spec.get("evidence") or "its job"
        out.append(f"**EPHEMERAL.** Written for {ticket} and rendered into that job; "
                   "not a ratified skill, never committed to a repository's .claude/skills/. "
                   "It expires with the job.")
        out.append("")
    if brief.get("why"):
        out.append(f"**Why this exists:** {brief['why'].strip()}")
        out.append("")
    out.append(f"GENERATED from `{src}` by `hee-gen-skills`. Do not edit this file;")
    out.append("edit the Skill object and regenerate. A hand-edit here is lost on the")
    out.append("next run and, worse, silently disagrees with the object until then.")
    out.append("")

    for key, heading in HEADINGS.items():
        if key not in spec:
            continue
        if key == "procedure":
            out.append(f"## {heading}")
            out.append("")
            out.extend(render_procedure(spec[key], brief))
            out.append("")
            continue
        out.append(f"## {heading}")
        out.append("")
        out.extend(as_lines(spec[key]))
        out.append("")

    # Anything the object carries that this tool has no heading for is still
    # emitted. Dropping unknown fields silently is how a generator quietly
    # loses content the source considered worth recording.
    extra = [k for k in spec if k not in HEADINGS and k not in ("agent_brief", "ephemeral")]
    if extra:
        out.append("## Other fields from the Skill object")
        out.append("")
        for k in extra:
            out.append(f"### {k.replace('_', ' ')}")
            out.append("")
            out.extend(as_lines(spec[k]))
            out.append("")
    return "\n".join(out).rstrip() + "\n"


def resolve_repo(argv):
    """--repo DIR, else the git repository the cwd is inside, else the
    engine checkout this tool is installed in. The install path is the
    LAST resort, not the first: that ordering is the whole fix."""
    if "--repo" in argv:
        return Path(argv[argv.index("--repo") + 1]).expanduser().resolve()
    try:
        top = subprocess.run(["git", "rev-parse", "--show-toplevel"], capture_output=True,
                             text=True, check=False)
        if top.returncode == 0 and top.stdout.strip():
            return Path(top.stdout.strip()).resolve()
    except OSError:
        pass
    return INSTALL_ROOT


def load(src):
    try:
        doc = yaml.safe_load(src.read_text())
    except (OSError, yaml.YAMLError) as e:
        print(f"hee-gen-skills: cannot parse {src}: {e}", file=sys.stderr)
        return None, 2
    if not isinstance(doc, dict) or doc.get("kind") != "Skill":
        kind = doc.get("kind") if isinstance(doc, dict) else type(doc).__name__
        print(f"hee-gen-skills: {src} is kind={kind}, not Skill -- skipped")
        return None, 0
    if not skill_name(doc):
        print(f"hee-gen-skills: {src} has no metadata.name", file=sys.stderr)
        return None, 2
    return doc, 0


def emit(doc, src_label, outdir, write, show_root):
    """Render one object to outdir/<name>/SKILL.md. Returns (changed, rc)."""
    try:
        body = render(doc, src_label)
    except (TypeError, ValueError) as e:
        print(f"hee-gen-skills: {e}", file=sys.stderr)
        return False, 2
    dest = outdir / skill_name(doc) / "SKILL.md"
    try:
        shown = dest.relative_to(show_root)
    except ValueError:
        shown = dest
    current = dest.read_text() if dest.exists() else None
    if current == body:
        print(f"hee-gen-skills: unchanged  {shown}")
        return False, 0
    if write:
        dest.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
        dest.write_text(body)
        print(f"hee-gen-skills: {'wrote' if current is None else 'updated'}     {shown}")
    else:
        print(f"hee-gen-skills: {'would create' if current is None else 'would update'} {shown}")
    return True, 0


def value_after(argv, flag):
    out = []
    for i, a in enumerate(argv):
        if a == flag:
            if i + 1 >= len(argv):
                print(f"hee-gen-skills: {flag} needs a value", file=sys.stderr)
                return None
            out.append(argv[i + 1])
    return out


def main():
    argv = sys.argv[1:]
    if help_wanted(argv):
        note_ignored(argv)
        print(__doc__)
        return 0
    write = "--write" in argv
    for flag in ("--repo", "--out", "--skill"):
        if value_after(argv, flag) is None:
            return 3
    skills = [Path(p).expanduser() for p in value_after(argv, "--skill")]
    outs = value_after(argv, "--out")
    cwd = Path.cwd()

    if skills:
        if not outs:
            print("hee-gen-skills: --skill needs --out DIR (the job's skills directory)",
                  file=sys.stderr)
            return 3
        outdir = Path(outs[-1]).expanduser()
        changed = 0
        for src in skills:
            if not src.is_file():
                print(f"hee-gen-skills: no such file {src}", file=sys.stderr)
                return 2
            doc, rc = load(src)
            if rc:
                return rc
            if doc is None:
                continue
            # The GENERATED banner must read the same from a test, a CI
            # example and a shell: relative to where the tool runs, never an
            # absolute path that differs per machine.
            try:
                label = src.resolve().relative_to(cwd)
            except ValueError:
                label = src
            did, rc = emit(doc, label, outdir, write, cwd)
            if rc:
                return rc
            changed += did
        if changed and not write:
            print(f"hee-gen-skills: {changed} file(s) differ. Re-run with --write to apply.")
            return 1
        return 0

    repo = resolve_repo(argv)
    outdir = Path(outs[-1]).expanduser() if outs else repo / ".claude" / "skills"
    skills_dir = repo / "hee" / "skills"
    if not skills_dir.is_dir():
        print(f"hee-gen-skills: no {skills_dir}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 3

    srcs = sorted(skills_dir.glob("*.yaml"))
    if not srcs:
        print("hee-gen-skills: no Skill objects found")
        return 0

    changed = 0
    for src in srcs:
        doc, rc = load(src)
        if rc:
            return rc
        if doc is None:
            continue
        if is_ephemeral(doc):
            print(f"hee-gen-skills: {src.relative_to(repo)} is labelled ephemeral; "
                  "hee/skills/ is the ratified tree. Render it with --skill into its job.",
                  file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
        did, rc = emit(doc, src.relative_to(repo), outdir, write, repo)
        if rc:
            return rc
        changed += did

    if changed and not write:
        print(f"hee-gen-skills: {changed} file(s) differ. Re-run with --write to apply.")
        return 1
    return 0


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
